hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15585","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Israil narrated to us, from Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, from al-Saib ibn Abdullah, he said: I was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah, Uthman ibn Affan and Zuhayr brought me. They began praising him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Do not inform me of him, he was my companion in Jahiliyyah. He said: He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, what a good companion you were. He said: So he said: O Saib, look at the morals you used to do in Jahiliyyah, make them in Islam: acknowledge the guest, honor the orphan, and do good to the neighbour."
"15586","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Muhajir, narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Qaid al-Saib, from al-Saib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The prayer of one sitting is upon half of the prayer of one standing."
"15587","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Qaid al-Saib, from al-Saib, that he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): You were my partner, you were the best partner, you did not evade nor dispute."
"15588","Rawh narrated to us: Sayf narrated to us, he said: I heard Mujahid saying: al-Saib ibn Abi al-Saib al-Abidi was the partner of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Jahiliyyah. He said: So he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah and said: By my father and mother, you do not evade nor dispute."
"15589","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Thabit, meaning Abu Zayd, narrated to us: Hilal, meaning Ibn Khabbab, narrated to us, from Mujahid, from his mawla, that he narrated to him that he was among those building the Kaaba in Jahiliyyah. He said: I had a stone I carved with my hands, worshipping it besides Allah the Blessed and Exalted. I would bring thick milk which I begrudged myself, and pour it upon it. A dog would come and lick it, then raise its leg and urinate. We built until we reached the place of the Stone, and none saw the Stone. It was amidst our stones like the head of a man, the face of a man almost visible from it. A tribe of Quraysh said: We shall place it, and others said: We shall place it. They said: Make a judge between you. They said: The first man to come forth from the pass. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came. They said: The Trustworthy came to you. They said to him. So he placed it in a garment, then called their tribes, and they took its sides with him. He placed it, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"15590","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Mujahid, from al-Saib ibn Abi al-Saib, that he used to share with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before Islam in trade. When it was the day of the Conquest, he came to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Welcome to my brother and my partner, he did not evade nor dispute. O Saib, you used to do deeds in Jahiliyyah not accepted from you, and today they are accepted from you. And he was of precedence and kinship."
